IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore) -- section 7A (the solvency statement) and
-- section 10 (who may be a company's auditor).
--
-- These are the two operative provisions that sit inside the definitional core:
-- s 7A is the gate to three of the Act's capital operations, and s 10 is the gate to
-- every audit the Act requires.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.

§ `Companies Act 1967 -- ss 7A and 10`

§§ `7A(1) -- what the directors must be of the opinion`

-- s 7A(1): "'solvency statement', in relation to a proposed redemption of preference
-- shares by a company out of its capital under section 70, a proposed giving of
-- financial assistance by a company under section 76(9A) or (9B) or a proposed
-- reduction by a company of its share capital under section 78B or 78C, means a
-- statement by the directors of the company that they have formed the opinion --
--   (a) that, as regards the company's situation at the date of the statement, there is
--       NO GROUND on which the company could then be found to be UNABLE TO PAY ITS DEBTS;
--   (b) where --
--       (i) it is intended to commence winding up of the company within the period of
--           12 months immediately after the date of the statement, that the company will
--           be able to pay its debts IN FULL within the period of 12 months after the
--           date of commencement of the winding up; or
--       (ii) it is not intended so to commence winding up, that the company will be able
--            to pay its debts AS THEY FALL DUE during the period of 12 months
--            immediately after the date of the statement; and
--   (c) that the value of the company's assets is NOT LESS THAN the value of its
--       liabilities (including contingent liabilities) AND WILL NOT, after the proposed
--       redemption, giving of financial assistance or reduction (as the case may be),
--       become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)".
--
-- Limb (b) is a fork on intention. Intending to wind up within a year moves the test
-- from "pay debts as they fall due for 12 months" to "pay debts in full within 12
-- months of the winding up commencing".
DECLARE ProposedOperation IS ONE OF
    `redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`
    `financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
    `reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C`
    `something else`

DECLARE SolvencyOpinion HAS
    `the operation it is for` IS A ProposedOperation
    `no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is intended to commence winding up within 12 months after the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of the winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months after the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the assets is now not less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the assets will not, after the proposed operation, become less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the opinion` IS A SolvencyOpinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is one a solvency statement is defined for` IF
    CONSIDER `the opinion`'s `the operation it is for`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the opinion` IS A SolvencyOpinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (b) of the opinion is held` IF
    IF   `the opinion`'s `it is intended to commence winding up within 12 months after the date of the statement`
    THEN `the opinion`'s `the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of the winding up`
    ELSE `the opinion`'s `the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months after the date of the statement`

GIVEN `the opinion` IS A SolvencyOpinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors hold all three opinions section 7A(1) requires` IF
        `the opinion`'s `no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts`
    AND `limb (b) of the opinion is held` `the opinion`
    AND `the opinion`'s `the value of the assets is now not less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities`
    AND `the opinion`'s `the value of the assets will not, after the proposed operation, become less than the value of the liabilities including contingent liabilities`

§§ `7A(2) -- the form of the statement`

-- s 7A(2): "The solvency statement --
--   (a) if the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C,
--       must be in the form of a written declaration signed by EVERY director; or
--   (b) if the company is not such a company, must be in the form of a written
--       declaration signed by every director OR must be ACCOMPANIED BY A REPORT FROM ITS
--       AUDITOR that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of
--       the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances."
--
-- THE ASYMMETRY. A small company that is exempt from audit has one way to give a
-- solvency statement: every director signs. A company that is not exempt has two: every
-- director signs, or an auditor's report accompanies it. So the company with the least
-- machinery is held to the stricter formality. The words of (b) also leave open whether,
-- on the auditor's-report route, the statement must still be a signed declaration by
-- anyone; the encoding reads the route as a substitute for unanimity, which is the
-- only reading under which it is an alternative.
DECLARE StatementForm HAS
    `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors who signed the written declaration` IS A NUMBER
    `an auditor's report accompanies it saying the auditor has inquired into the company's affairs and thinks the statement not unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the form` IS A StatementForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every director signed` IF
    `the form`'s `the number of directors who signed the written declaration` AT LEAST `the form`'s `the number of directors`

GIVEN `the form` IS A StatementForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is in a form section 7A(2) allows` IF
    IF   `the form`'s `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`
    THEN `every director signed` `the form`
    ELSE     `every director signed` `the form`
         OR  `the form`'s `an auditor's report accompanies it saying the auditor has inquired into the company's affairs and thinks the statement not unreasonable`

§§ `7A(3), (4), (5) -- how the directors must go about forming the opinion`

-- s 7A(3): "the directors of the company MUST TAKE INTO ACCOUNT ALL LIABILITIES of the
-- company (including contingent liabilities)."
-- s 7A(4): in determining whether assets are or will become less than liabilities the
-- directors --
--   (a) MUST HAVE REGARD TO (i) the most recent financial statements of the company that
--       comply with section 201(2) and (5), and (ii) all other circumstances that the
--       directors KNOW OR OUGHT TO KNOW affect, or may affect, the value of the assets and
--       liabilities; and
--   (b) MAY RELY ON valuations of assets or estimates of liabilities that are reasonable
--       in the circumstances.
-- s 7A(5): in valuing a contingent liability the directors MAY take into account (a) the
-- likelihood of the contingency occurring, and (b) any claim the company is entitled to
-- make and can reasonably expect to be met to reduce or extinguish it.
--
-- These are conduct requirements for forming the opinion. They are recorded as a record
-- of what the directors did, because the offence in s 7A(6) turns on whether they had
-- reasonable grounds, and these are what the grounds are made of.
DECLARE HowTheOpinionWasFormed HAS
    `took into account all liabilities including contingent liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had regard to the most recent financial statements complying with section 201(2) and (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had regard to all other circumstances the directors know or ought to know affect the value of assets and liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relied on valuations or estimates that were reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `how` IS A HowTheOpinionWasFormed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors went about forming the opinion as section 7A(3) and (4)(a) require` IF
        `how`'s `took into account all liabilities including contingent liabilities`
    AND `how`'s `had regard to the most recent financial statements complying with section 201(2) and (5)`
    AND `how`'s `had regard to all other circumstances the directors know or ought to know affect the value of assets and liabilities`

§§ `7A(6) -- the offence`

-- s 7A(6): "A director of a company who makes a solvency statement WITHOUT HAVING
-- REASONABLE GROUNDS for the opinions expressed in it shall be guilty of an offence and
-- shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 3 years or to both."
--
-- The offence is made by each director who makes the statement. It is not confined to
-- a statement that turns out to be wrong, and it is not made out merely by the company
-- later failing; the question is the reasonableness of the grounds when it was made.
-- The statutory duty to take all liabilities into account, and to have regard to what
-- the directors know or ought to know, gives the content of the grounds.
`the maximum fine under section 7A(6), in dollars` MEANS 100000
`the maximum imprisonment under section 7A(6), in months` MEANS 36

DECLARE DirectorsStatement HAS
    `this director made the solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the company later became insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the director` IS A DirectorsStatement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director commits the offence in section 7A(6)` IF
        `the director`'s `this director made the solvency statement`
    AND NOT `the director`'s `this director had reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it`

-- Later insolvency is not an element, which is the point of the cases that use it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a later insolvency is an element of the offence` IF
    FALSE

§§ `10 -- who may be a company's auditor`

-- s 10(1): "No person OTHER THAN AN ACCOUNTING ENTITY may -- (a) KNOWINGLY consent to be
-- appointed as auditor for a company; or (b) KNOWINGLY act as an auditor for a company."
-- s 10(2): "Without limiting subsection (1)(b), a person acts as an auditor for a company
-- if the person PREPARES ANY REPORT required by this Act to be prepared by an auditor of
-- the company."
-- s 4(1): "'accounting entity' means a public accountant, an accounting corporation, an
-- accounting firm or an accounting limited liability partnership".
--
-- Both prohibitions carry "knowingly". s 10 itself states no penalty; the Act's general
-- penalty provisions were not read.
DECLARE Auditor IS ONE OF
    `a public accountant`
    `an accounting corporation`
    `an accounting firm`
    `an accounting limited liability partnership`
    `not an accounting entity`

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Auditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an accounting entity` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `not an accounting entity` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Auditor,
      `consents or acts knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 10(1)` IF
        NOT `the person is an accounting entity` `the person`
    AND `consents or acts knowingly`

-- s 10(2): preparing an auditor's report is acting as an auditor.
GIVEN `the person prepared a report the Act requires an auditor to prepare` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person acted as an auditor` IF
    `the person prepared a report the Act requires an auditor to prepare`

§§ `10(3), (4) -- the entity's prior consent`

-- s 10(3): "No company or person may appoint an accounting entity as an auditor of a
-- company WITHOUT OBTAINING THE ACCOUNTING ENTITY'S PRIOR CONSENT."
-- s 10(4): for the purposes of (3), the consent --
--   (a) of a public accountant must be in writing signed by the public accountant;
--   (b) of an accounting firm, or an accounting limited liability partnership, must be in
--       writing signed by at least ONE PARTNER of the firm or limited liability
--       partnership; and
--   (c) of an accounting corporation must be in writing signed by at least ONE DIRECTOR of
--       the corporation.
DECLARE Consent HAS
    `who is being appointed` IS AN Auditor
    `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was signed by the public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of partners who signed` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors who signed` IS A NUMBER
    `it was obtained before the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent is signed as section 10(4) requires` IF
    CONSIDER `the consent`'s `who is being appointed`
    WHEN `a public accountant` THEN `the consent`'s `it was signed by the public accountant`
    WHEN `an accounting firm` THEN `the consent`'s `the number of partners who signed` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `an accounting limited liability partnership` THEN `the consent`'s `the number of partners who signed` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `an accounting corporation` THEN `the consent`'s `the number of directors who signed` AT LEAST 1
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment complies with section 10(3) and (4)` IF
        `the consent`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `the consent is signed as section 10(4) requires` `the consent`
    AND `the consent`'s `it was obtained before the appointment`

§§ `10(5), (6) -- who is appointed when a firm or a corporation is appointed in its own name`

-- s 10(5): "Where an accounting firm is appointed as auditor of the company in the name of
-- the accounting firm, the appointment takes effect and operates as if the PARTNERS OF
-- THE FIRM AT THE TIME OF THE APPOINTMENT, who are public accountants AT THAT TIME, are
-- appointed as auditors of the company."
-- s 10(6): "Where an accounting corporation is appointed as auditor of the company in the
-- name of the corporation, the appointment takes effect and operates as if --
--   (a) the directors of the corporation who are practising as public accountants in the
--       corporation (WHETHER DIRECTORS AT THE TIME the accounting corporation was
--       appointed as auditor OR LATER); and
--   (b) the employees of the corporation who are practising as public accountants in the
--       corporation (WHETHER EMPLOYED AT THE TIME ... OR LATER),
-- are appointed as auditors of the company."
--
-- THE TWO RULES DIFFER, AND NEITHER SAYS WHY.
--   * A firm's appointment is fixed at the moment of appointment: only partners then in
--     the firm and then public accountants are the auditors. A partner admitted later is
--     not an auditor of the company, and a partner who qualifies as a public accountant
--     later is not either.
--   * A corporation's appointment runs forward: directors and employees who join later are
--     auditors too.
--
-- AND THERE IS A GAP. s 10(4)(b) treats an accounting limited liability partnership like a
-- firm for the form of consent, and s 4(1) makes it an accounting entity, but neither
-- s 10(5) nor s 10(6) mentions it. If an accounting limited liability partnership is
-- appointed in its own name, no provision says which individuals are appointed.
DECLARE Practitioner IS ONE OF
    `a partner of the accounting firm`
    `a director of the accounting corporation`
    `an employee of the accounting corporation`
    `a partner of the accounting limited liability partnership`
    `someone else`

DECLARE PractitionerFacts HAS
    `role` IS A Practitioner
    `is practising as a public accountant in the entity now` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held that role at the time of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a public accountant at the time of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the practitioner` IS A PractitionerFacts, `the entity appointed in its own name` IS AN Auditor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practitioner is appointed as an auditor through the entity` IF
    CONSIDER `the entity appointed in its own name`
    WHEN `an accounting firm`
        THEN     (`the practitioner`'s `role` EQUALS `a partner of the accounting firm`)
             AND `the practitioner`'s `held that role at the time of the appointment`
             AND `the practitioner`'s `was a public accountant at the time of the appointment`
    WHEN `an accounting corporation`
        THEN     (    `the practitioner`'s `role` EQUALS `a director of the accounting corporation`
                  OR  `the practitioner`'s `role` EQUALS `an employee of the accounting corporation`)
             AND `the practitioner`'s `is practising as a public accountant in the entity now`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The gap, stated as a function so it can be asserted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10 says who is appointed when an accounting limited liability partnership is appointed in its own name` IF
    FALSE
